 for(let i=-1;i<=1;i+=2){let wx=x+i*w*.24,wz=z+d/2+.03;poly([[wx-.5,1.2,wz],[wx+.5,1.2,wz],[wx+.5,2.4,wz],[wx-.5,2.4,wz]],'#120e11'); // boarded cross
  ctx.strokeStyle='#5a4636';line...}
 // exposed beams on top
 ctx.strokeStyle='#191113';lines from ...
 // vines
}
```
But the south face of neighbor ruins at z+d/2 is facing street; camera at z 20+ sees them. fine.

Add warm lit window for one: fill one pane orange.

drawScrapCar:
```js
function drawScrapCar(o){let {x,z,w,d}=o,b=o.burnt;let c=b?'#2c2324':'#3f3a35';
 boxAt(x,z,w,d,.55,c,'#1b1517',b?'#3a2a26':'#4e463c');
 boxAt(x,z-d*.15,w*.88,d*.5,.55,'#241d1e','#151012','#31231f'); // cabin
 // wheels
 ...
 // broken window
 poly(...dark)
 // rust streaks
}
```

drawPole: box thin with crossarm; lamp head small box at y=h-0.4; plus light glow handled.
Add cables drawn separately using poles: collect scenery poles sorted and draw quadratic curves between tops (screen space). With just two poles, draw one cable each direction and a hanging line; plus wires continue offscreen? Fine.

drawBarrel: box + fire (animated ellipses with time). Also smoke.

drawRubble: 4-6 small boxes/triangles at offsets, some with rebar lines.

drawGate: stone posts and iron bars:
```js
function drawGate(o){let x=o.x,z=o.z;
 boxAt(x-.15,z,.5,.5,1.9,'#4a3f36','#2e2622','#7b6350');
 // bars fanning open toward street: from post top to x±1.4,z+.9
 for(let i=0;i<5;i++){let t=i/4; line from (x, .2+i*.32, z) to (x+ (x<0?-1.4:1.4)*?,...) } 
```
Simpler draw bars along a diagonal line in world: endpoints post base (x, 0.15, z) to (x+dir*1.6, 0.15, z+1.1); vertical bars at interpolated points with heights 1.2. Use lines via project.

```js
let dir=o.x>0?1:-1;
for(let i=0;i<6;i++){let t=i/5,bx=x+dir*1.5*t,bz=z+.9*t;line base(0.1) to top(1.35)}
// top rail line
```
Looks like open gate.

drawFence: posts every 1.2 along x and two horizontal rails at y .5,1.0; metal dark.

drawTree: trunk box + branches lines; dead or foliage blobs. Use projected strokes with dark color, maybe silhouette. Add branches at various heights.

drawWires: between pole tops (h-0.2), sag mid. Use screen coordinates; ctx.strokeStyle dark. If any behind camera skip.

drawLamps: additive glow. Need time for flicker. Use `let fl= l.flick? .82+.18*Math.sin(time*12+l.x*3)+.06*Math.sin(time*31):1`.

```js
function drawLamps(){ctx.save();ctx.globalCompositeOperation='lighter';for(let l of lamps){let p=project(l.x,l.y,l.z);if(p.d<.3)continue;let r=Math.max(20,l.r*Math.min(W,H)*.92/p.d);let fl=...;let g=ctx.createRadialGradient(p.x,p.y,1,p.x,p.y,r);g.addColorStop(0,`rgba(${l.c},${.2*l.i*fl})`);g.addColorStop(.35,`rgba(${l.c},${.08*l.i*fl})`);g.addColorStop(1,`rgba(${l.c},0)`);ctx.fillStyle=g;ctx.beginPath();ctx.arc(p.x,p.y,r,0,Math.PI*2);ctx.fill()}ctx.restore()}
```
Radius formula: l.r (world units) * focal / depth. focal = min(W,H)*.92. Use that. Cap to 1.6*min dimension.

Note: this draws glows over HUD? HUD is DOM above canvas, so fine.

drawSmoke: for barrels and one ruin, project source (x,1.2,z), then loop 5 puffs at y 1.2+i*.7 offset time; alpha decreasing. Use 'source-over' gray.

Draw lamps after drawGrade maybe; after grade so they pop. drawSmoke before grade? Smoke should be graded; draw before grade. Order in render: world → drawWires → drawGable → drawPlayer → drawLight → drawLamps → drawSmoke? Smoke should be behind player? It's ambient; draw before player. Let's do: renderables → drawWires → drawGable → drawSmoke → drawPlayer → drawLight → drawLamps → drawGrade → shake.

Rugs drawn after floor before shadows.

